<title>SINGAPORE: IDT hits high of US$1.05 at debut.</title>
<headline>IDT hits high of US$1.05 at debut.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Liquid crystal consumer products maker IDT Holdings Ltd debut at a high of US$1.05 against its initial offer price of US$0.73 on Monday.  </p>
<p>After about 10 minutes of trading, the share was hovering around US$0.945 after hitting a low of US$0.935. Volume was over 5.9 million units.</p>
<p>The company, a unit of Hong Kong's IDT International, had offered a total of 22.08 million shares in its Singapore IPO.</p>
<p>The offer ws 41 times subscribed.</p>
<p>The company planned to use the IPO proceeds of US$7.1 million to expand its facilities in China.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
